# Forth system context (not challenge coding)

Use this file to **route** questions. It does **not** replace stack/style rules for writing colon definitions.

## Two kinds of tasks

| Kind | User intent (signals) | Use | Do **not** default to |
|------|----------------------|-----|------------------------|
| **Code / challenge** | implement word, fix `.fs`, stack effect, refactor, test failure, LeetCode-style task | `forth-stack`, `forth-style`, `forth-control`, `forth-factoring`, `forth-dialect-gforth`, other `forth-*.mdc` | Long FMAP essays unless porting or target is explicit |
| **System / niche / architecture** | choose Forth for project, embedded vs hosted, ITC vs STC, Harvard, co-design, portability layers, domain dialect (FORTH-X), “why Forth on MCU/FPGA”, training tags for target | Human docs below + `data/forth-*.json` | Inventing platform facts; mixing Gforth desktop idioms into embedded without FMAP tag |

When **both** apply (e.g. port `: sort` to STM8), start from **code rules**, then pull **only** the platform slice from architecture docs (FMAP profile, missing wordsets).

## Layer model (short)

| Layer | What | Doc |
|-------|------|-----|
| **0** | Domain dialect **FORTH-X** (syntax facade → dictionary) | `docs/FORTH-DIALECT-LAYERS.md` |
| **1** | ANS algorithms | `docs/FORTH-ANS-PORTABILITY-LAYER.md`, `forth-portability.mdc` |
| **2** | Adapters / compat shims | `docs/FORTH-ANS-PORTABILITY-LAYER.md` |
| **3** | Platform: FMAP, prim, cross, hardware | `docs/FORTH-SYSTEM-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/FORTH-HARDWARE-CODESIGN.md` |

**FORTH-&lt;domain&gt;** (e.g. FORTH-BASIC, FORTH-HDL) is an **idiomatic Forth pattern**: parsing/compile words + spec + environmental dependency — not a separate VM. See layer 0 doc; implementation mechanics — `forth-meta.mdc`, `forth-defining.mdc`.

